      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not sure emplace_back() buys us anything here. (We\u0027ll be using the copy constructor for std::array\u003c\u003e either way.)\n\n\nThe benefit of emplace_back() is avoiding the creation of a temporary. E.g.\n\n  legacy_addrs.push_back(std::array\u003cuint8_t, 6\u003e{1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6});\n\nIf we use emplace_back in that case:\n\n  legacy_addrs.emplace_back(1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6);\n\nthen we avoid creating a temporary array.\n\n\nBut, in our case, we\u0027ve already got an array (the array referenced by |addr|). So there\u0027s no temporary to optimize out.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 193,
        "startChar": 17,
        "endLine": 193,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "752f5150ae0c4f39d0df9daa02caaae9dda8ec6f",
